Straw man. It is possible; it is sometimes very unlikely. The first time
you claim a very unlikely event has happened, fine. But when you claim a
long series of very unlikely events, I start looking for another
explanation.

If I were to tell you that I had rolled 2d6 and they'd come up double-6,
you'd believe me. If I were to tell you that I'd made thousands of rolls
and one in 3 were double-6, you'd either claim I was lying about what I
observed (and I am not claiming that about you) or that some other factor
was at work - crooked dice, say, or a failure on my part to read the dice
correctly.

As I mentioned; the last time I provided a definitive account of the
probability of something that you claimed happened on a regular basis, it
turned out to be quite improbable that it had ever happened at all. At
that point you turned out to have been talking about something else
entirely. Do you see why I tend to be a bit skeptical when you tell us yet
another improbable thing happened?
